.TH SYSINFO-VLHE 1 "2026-10-03" "VLHE 1.0" "VLHE Manual"
.SH NAME
sysinfo-vlhe \- write a report of this machine and VLHE, to send when something goes wrong
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysinfo-vlhe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysinfo-vlhe
reports what VLHE can see on this machine, writes the report to a
file, and shows it on the screen. It is the file to send with a
problem report.
.PP
The report covers the kernel version and how it was built; this copy
of VLHE, its version, and where it runs from; which sound modules are
loaded, and the boot files
.IR /etc/modules ,
.I /etc/conf.modules
and
.IR /etc/devices ;
the sound and CD-ROM device nodes, including where
.I /dev/dsp
and
.I /dev/cdrom
point; VLHE's daemons, virtual drives, mixer levels and the SoundFont
files it can find; where its configuration files are; the session
file; and the end of the daemon log.
.PP
It changes nothing on the machine. The only other file it writes is
a scratch file under
.IR /tmp .
It never reads
.IR /proc/sound ,
which can crash a 2.2 kernel on a machine with several sound cards.
.PP
Run as root it can also report what only root can read. As root it
ignores the
.B VLHE_*
environment variables, as
.B vlhe
and
.B vlhe.gtk
do, so the report describes what root's VLHE uses; any that were set
are named in the report.
.PP
.B Read the report before sending it.
It can contain your user name, your home directory, and the names and
paths of your files, such as disc images and SoundFonts.
.PP
It is not on the
.BR PATH .
An installed VLHE keeps it in
.IR /usr/local/share/vlhe/tools/ ,
the package in
.IR /usr/share/vlhe/tools/ ,
and a portable folder in its
.I tools/
folder.
.SH OPTIONS
None. Any argument prints a usage message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I sysinfo-vlhe-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.txt
The report, written in the current directory, or in
.I /tmp
if the current directory cannot be written. The last line on the
screen names it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was made. If no file could be written, the report is shown
on the screen only, and it says so.
.TP
.B 1
An argument was given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
cd
.br
/usr/local/share/vlhe/tools/sysinfo-vlhe
.RE
